# =============================================================================
# Per-Dockerfile ignore for process-management/Dockerfile.api
#
# The build context is the repo root (jxt-evidence-system/). This Dockerfile
# COPYs TWO trees:
#   - process-management/   (the service source)
#   - jxt-core/             (local checkout; go.mod uses
#                            `replace github.com/ChenBigdata421/jxt-core => ../jxt-core`,
#                            which resolves to /jxt-core inside the image)
#
# The repo-root .dockerignore is tuned for the jxt-benchmark build and excludes
# BOTH process-management/ and jxt-core/, which would otherwise empty this
# build's context (and break the local-jxt-core COPY).
#
# BuildKit gives <Dockerfile-name>.dockerignore precedence over the root
# .dockerignore, so here we re-include the process-management/ and jxt-core/
# trees and keep every unrelated sibling excluded to keep the context small.
# tests/ is intentionally included: go.work uses ./tests, so the build runs in
# workspace mode and needs the tests module in context.
# The jxt-benchmark build is untouched — it still uses the root .dockerignore.
# =============================================================================

# Exclude everything under the repo root ...
*
# ... then re-include only the trees this Dockerfile COPYs.
!process-management
!process-management/**
!jxt-core
!jxt-core/**

# Universal cruft inside the included trees (never needed to compile).
process-management/.git
process-management/**/.git/
process-management/**/node_modules/
jxt-core/.git
jxt-core/**/.git/
jxt-core/**/node_modules/
